.TH hsh 1 "2026-02-19" "version 1.0" "Simple Shell Manual"
.SH NAME
hsh \- simple UNIX command line interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hsh
.RI [ options ] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B hsh
program is a simple shell that reads and executes commands from the user. Commands can be given with absolute path or using the PATH environment variable.

It supports the following built-in command:

.TP
.B exit
Exit the shell. Exits with the status of the last executed command.

.SH USAGE
In interactive mode, the shell displays a prompt ":)" and waits for user input:

.RS
$ ./hsh
:) /bin/ls
file1  file2
:)
.RE

Non-interactive mode:

.RS
$ echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
file1  file2
.RE

Errors are printed in the format:

.RS
./hsh: 1: command: not found
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
if the shell exits normally.
.B 127
if a command cannot be found.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
The shell uses the standard UNIX environment variables, including
.B PATH
for locating executables.

